    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Capital distributions to NextEra Energy Transmission LLC and/or GridLiance Holdco LP and/or GridLiance Eastern Holdings LLC.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Charges based on annual Transmission Revenue Requirement as approved by the FERC.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Charges based on various point to point connections.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">General accumulated provision for depreciation of electric utility plant relate to the Company's distribution plant services.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">GridLiance Management, LLC ("ManageCo") provides corporate services on an as-needed basis, including but not limited to, corporate oversight, human resources, records management, risk management, and payroll services at cost. The Company allocated indirect costs from ManageCo based on the Company's "Direct Charge" cost allocation methodology which is based on a proportional ratio of direct charges to each affiliate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Services provided by affiliated companies may include executive &amp; governance, finance &amp; accounting, corporate communications, legal, corporate real estate, human resources, payroll, security, internal audit, information management operations and maintenance, and license fees. Services are allocated to affiliates using specific drivers such as headcount or number of workstations. If cost cannot be attributed, the services are allocated using the Massachusetts Formula.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Services provided by affiliated companies may include executive &amp; governance, finance &amp; accounting, corporate communications, legal, corporate real estate, human resources, payroll, security, internal audit, information management operations and maintenance, and license fees. Services are allocated to affiliates using specific drivers such as headcount or number of workstations. If cost cannot be attributed, the services are allocated using the Massachusetts Formula.</link:footnote>
